---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { product } from "../data/product";
import { company } from "../data/company";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description={`How ${product.name} handles information — version ${product.legalDocsVersion.privacy}.`}
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pt-16 pb-20">
    <header>
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-indigo-700 uppercase tracking-wide">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-500">
        {product.name} · Version {product.legalDocsVersion.privacy} · Last updated:{" "}
        {product.legalDocsVersion.lastUpdated}
      </p>
      <div class="mt-5 rounded-lg border border-indigo-200 bg-indigo-50/40 p-4 text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
        <strong class="text-slate-900">Summary.</strong>
        {product.name} stores core study data on your device using SQLite and MMKV, uses Firebase
        Analytics for pseudonymous usage analytics and Firebase Crashlytics for crash diagnostics,
        and uses RevenueCat to validate subscription status. We do not ask you to create an account
        and we do not directly collect your name, email address, or phone number inside the App.
      </div>
    </header>

    <nav aria-label="Table of contents" class="mt-10 rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-5">
      <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold text-slate-700 uppercase tracking-wide">Contents</h2>
      <ul class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-indigo-700">
        <li><a class="hover:underline" href="#scope">1. Scope of This Policy</a></li>
        <li><a class="hover:underline" href="#collect">2. Information We Collect</a></li>
        <li><a class="hover:underline" href="#use">3. How We Use Information</a></li>
        <li><a class="hover:underline" href="#share">4. How Information Is Shared</a></li>
        <li><a class="hover:underline" href="#retention">5. Data Retention and Deletion</a></li>
        <li><a class="hover:underline" href="#rights">6. Your Rights and Choices</a></li>
        <li><a class="hover:underline" href="#children">7. Children's Privacy</a></li>
        <li><a class="hover:underline" href="#security">8. Security</a></li>
        <li><a class="hover:underline" href="#changes">9. Changes to This Policy</a></li>
        <li><a class="hover:underline" href="#contact">10. Contact Information</a></li>
      </ul>
    </nav>

    <div class="mt-10 space-y-10 text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
      <section id="scope">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900">1. Scope of This Policy</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          This Privacy Policy explains how {product.name} (the "App," "we," "us," or "our") handles
          information when you use the App. It covers data stored locally on your device and data
          processed by the third-party services we use to operate analytics, crash diagnostics,
          content delivery, and subscriptions.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="collect">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900">2. Information We Collect</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">We collect or process the following categories of information:</p>
        <div class="mt-4 overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-slate-200">
          <table class="w-full text-sm">
            <thead class="bg-slate-50">
              <tr>
                <th class="text-left font-semibold text-slate-700 px-4 py-3 align-top">Category</th>
                <th class="text-left font-semibold text-slate-700 px-4 py-3 align-top">What it includes</th>
                <th class="text-left font-semibold text-slate-700 px-4 py-3 align-top">Where it is stored</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-200">
              <tr>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top font-medium text-slate-900">Local study and app data</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top">
                  Learning progress, answered questions, review history, downloaded state selection,
                  onboarding status, language choices, subscription consent versions, and user
                  preferences.
                </td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top">On your device using SQLite and MMKV</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top font-medium text-slate-900">Analytics data</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top">
                  Device and app information such as device model, operating system, locale, app
                  opens, screen views, feature usage, and app event activity collected through
                  Firebase Analytics.
                </td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top">Processed by Firebase Analytics</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top font-medium text-slate-900">Crash diagnostics</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top">
                  Crash stack traces and device context collected through Firebase Crashlytics when
                  the App crashes, including two custom attributes: state code and content mode.
                </td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top">Processed by Firebase Crashlytics</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top font-medium text-slate-900">Subscription data</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top">
                  Subscription status, entitlement access, storefront or platform, transaction
                  status, and an app user identifier used to validate purchases via RevenueCat.
                </td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top">Processed by RevenueCat and the applicable app marketplace</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top font-medium text-slate-900">Content download logs</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top">
                  Standard HTTP request information (IP address, timestamp, requested file)
                  generated when the App downloads lesson content, images, or these legal
                  documents from our content delivery network. Not linked to any in-app
                  identifier.
                </td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 align-top">Processed by Cloudflare R2 (CDN)</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <h3 class="mt-6 text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">
          Information We Do Not Intentionally Collect Directly
        </h3>
        <p class="mt-3">
          The App does not require you to create an account, and we do not directly ask you to
          provide your name, email address, home address, phone number, or similar personal profile
          information inside the App.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Third-party service providers may receive technical identifiers or transaction-related
          data as part of their services. Those providers process data under their own agreements
          and policies.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="use">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900">3. How We Use Information</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">We use the information described above to:</p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
          <li>save your study progress, quiz history, settings, and language selections on your device;</li>
          <li>measure app usage, feature adoption, and product stability through Firebase Analytics;</li>
          <li>diagnose crashes and improve reliability through Firebase Crashlytics;</li>
          <li>verify subscription status and unlock paid features through RevenueCat;</li>
          <li>deliver lesson content and images to your device through our content delivery network;</li>
          <li>maintain legal consent records, such as the accepted Terms and Privacy Policy versions;</li>
          <li>improve the App, diagnose issues, and prioritize product updates.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="share">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900">4. How Information Is Shared</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We do not sell your personal information and we do not share personal information with
          third parties for cross-context behavioral advertising.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We share limited information only as needed with service providers that help operate the
          App:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
          <li><strong>Firebase Analytics</strong> for pseudonymous analytics and app measurement;</li>
          <li><strong>Firebase Crashlytics</strong> for crash diagnostics;</li>
          <li><strong>RevenueCat</strong> for subscription entitlement validation and purchase status;</li>
          <li>
            <strong>Cloudflare R2</strong> for content delivery (lessons, images, and legal
            documents); request logs include standard HTTP fields such as IP address;
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Apple App Store / Google Play</strong> to process in-app purchases and
            subscriptions.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <div class="mt-4 rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-4 text-sm text-slate-600">
          Most core study records remain local to your device unless a third-party service receives
          data that is necessary for analytics, crash diagnostics, content delivery, or
          subscription processing.
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="retention">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900">5. Data Retention and Deletion</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Local study data remains on your device until you clear the App's data, reset your device
          storage, or uninstall the App. If you remove the App, local SQLite and MMKV data stored
          by the App is generally deleted from the device.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Firebase Analytics, Firebase Crashlytics, RevenueCat, and Cloudflare may retain data
          according to their own retention policies and operational needs. We do not control those
          external retention periods directly.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="rights">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900">6. Your Rights and Choices</h2>

        <h3 class="mt-4 text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">General Choices</h3>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
          <li>You can stop using the App at any time.</li>
          <li>
            You can remove local App data by uninstalling the App or clearing device storage for
            the App.
          </li>
          <li>You can manage subscriptions through your Apple or Google Play account settings.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="mt-6 text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">EEA, UK, and Similar Privacy Rights</h3>
        <p class="mt-3">
          If local law applies, you may have rights to request access to, correction of, deletion
          of, or portability of personal data processed about you, and to object to or restrict
          certain processing. Because most learning data is stored only on your device, deletion is
          typically achieved by removing the App or clearing its local data.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          For users in the European Economic Area, United Kingdom, and similar jurisdictions, this
          section is intended to support rights commonly associated with the General Data
          Protection Regulation (GDPR) and comparable privacy laws.
        </p>

        <h3 class="mt-6 text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">California Privacy Notice</h3>
        <p class="mt-3">
          California users may have rights to know, access, delete, and correct personal
          information, subject to legal exceptions. We do not sell personal information and do not
          share personal information for cross-context behavioral advertising as part of the App's
          current MVP design.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          This California notice is intended to address rights commonly associated with the
          California Consumer Privacy Act and California Privacy Rights Act (CCPA/CPRA).
        </p>

        <p class="mt-3">
          For privacy requests or questions about third-party data handling, contact us using the
          email address below. If your request involves Firebase, RevenueCat, or Cloudflare data,
          we may need to direct you to the relevant provider or ask for additional details so we
          can understand the request.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="children">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900">7. Children's Privacy</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          The App is designed for learner drivers and is not intended for children under 13. We do
          not knowingly collect personal information directly from children under 13. If you are
          under 13, please use the App only with a parent or legal guardian's permission and
          supervision.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We intend this approach to align with the Children's Online Privacy Protection Act
          (COPPA) by avoiding direct collection of child-directed account information inside the
          App.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="security">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900">8. Security</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We use reasonable measures appropriate to the App's architecture to protect data handled
          by the App and our service providers. However, no app, device, transmission method, or
          storage system can be guaranteed to be completely secure.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="changes">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900">9. Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we do, we will revise the
          version number and "Last updated" date on this page. Material updates may also trigger a
          renewed consent flow inside the App.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="contact">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900">10. Contact Information</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          If you have privacy questions or requests, contact us at{" "}
          <a class="text-indigo-700 underline" href={`mailto:${product.emails.privacy}`}>
            {product.emails.privacy}
          </a>.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-4 rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-5 text-sm">
          <p class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Operator</p>
          <address class="not-italic mt-2 text-slate-700 leading-6">
            {company.legalName}<br />
            {company.address.line1}<br />
            {company.address.cityStateZip}<br />
            {company.address.country}
          </address>
          <p class="mt-3 text-slate-600">
            Illinois Limited Liability Company · IL File Number {company.ilFileNumber}
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>

    <footer class="mt-12 pt-6 border-t border-slate-200 text-sm text-slate-500">
      <p>
        {product.name} Privacy Policy · Version {product.legalDocsVersion.privacy}
      </p>
      <p>Last updated: {product.legalDocsVersion.lastUpdated}</p>
    </footer>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
